Survey complete. Findings:

## 1. `ZimmDrawer` (atom) — the canonical right-anchored drawer

`/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmDrawer/index.tsx`

**Prop surface** — base props + a three-member discriminated union for the accessible name:

```ts
type ZimmDrawerBaseProps = {
  isOpen: boolean;
  onClose: () => void;
  size: ZimmDrawerSize;
  children: React.ReactNode;
  titleStyle?: 'large' | 'small';
  finalFocusRef?: React.RefObject<HTMLElement>;
  initialFocusRef?: React.RefObject<HTMLElement>;
};

type ZimmDrawerProps = ZimmDrawerBaseProps &
  (
    | { title: string; labelledBy?: never; 'aria-label'?: never }
    | { title?: never; labelledBy: string; 'aria-label'?: never }
    | { title?: never; labelledBy?: never; 'aria-label': string }
  );
```

`export type ZimmDrawerSize = 'large' | 'tablet' | 'small' | 'xLarge' | 'mobile';`

**Right-anchoring** — no `placement` prop. It is hardcoded right-anchored in two places: `<Drawer ... placement="right">` (line 206) and the panel's own `__css={{ position: 'fixed', top: 0, right: 0, bottom: 0, ... }}` with framer-motion `initial={{ x: '100%' }} animate={{ x: 0 }} exit={{ x: '100%' }}`.

**Accessible name** — three mechanisms, set directly on `dialogProps` because Chakra's `getDialogProps` always recomputes `aria-labelledby` from a `<DrawerHeader>` that never mounts here:

```ts
const dialogProps = getDialogProps({ 'aria-label': ariaLabel });
if (title && titleId) {
  dialogProps['aria-labelledby'] = titleId;
} else if (labelledBy) {
  dialogProps['aria-labelledby'] = labelledBy;
}
```

`titleId` comes from `useId()`; the title renders as `<chakra.span id={titleId} ...>`.

**Close button** — not a Chakra `IconButton`; it's `ZimmButton` with a hardcoded English label, in both branches:

```tsx
<ZimmButton variant="icon" icon="close" label="Close" onClick={onClose} />
```

(Not localised — no `useIntl`/`useUiCopy` in this file. Contrast `zimmGalleryOverlay/index.tsx:192`, which does `label={intl.formatMessage(messages.close)}`.)

**Focus** — relies on Chakra, deliberately. It bypasses `<DrawerContent>` but reuses `useModalContext()` + `<ModalFocusScope>` so focus trap / initial focus / scroll lock / Escape all still come from Chakra. `initialFocusRef` is forwarded straight to `<Drawer>`. Focus return is the one hand-rolled piece:

```ts
// Chakra's FocusLock remains active during the exit animation, so any focus call made
// while the drawer is still mounted (rAF, close-button onClick) gets trapped and dropped.
const handleCloseComplete = () => {
  if (finalFocusRef) finalFocusRef.current?.focus();
};
```
wired as `onCloseComplete={handleCloseComplete}`. No `returnFocusOnClose` anywhere in the repo.

**Story portal assertion** — yes, `within(document.body)`, with a mandated inline comment:

`/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmDrawer/index.stories.tsx:36`
```ts
// Portal renders outside canvasElement — testing.md §Layer-2 exception. Chakra's Drawer is
// built on its Modal primitive, which renders DrawerContent via a Portal by default, so
// within(canvasElement) can't reach it.
const doc = within(document.body);
const dialog = await doc.findByRole('dialog');
await expect(dialog).toHaveAttribute('aria-label', 'Example drawer');
```
The title variant asserts by computed name instead: `await doc.findByRole('dialog', { name: 'SIGN IN' })`. Close stories use `await waitForElementToBeRemoved(dialog)` because of the exit animation.

Styling: `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmDrawer/zimmDrawer.css.ts` — `parts: ['overlay', 'content', 'closeButton', 'header', 'headerTitle']`, one variant per size. Note the comment at line 10 listing `Regional Storefront` and `Cookies` as *future* consumers of `small` (25%).

## 2. The other four

| Component | Path | test? | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ZimmPdpDrawer` | `.../ui-kits/organisms/zimmPdpDrawer/index.tsx` | **No** | Props `{isOpen, onClose, size, tabs, initialTabId?, ariaLabel}`. Passes `aria-label={ariaLabel}` to ZimmDrawer (no `title`), so keeps the floating close button. Stories assert via `within(document.body)` + `findByRole('dialog')`, plus tab/tabpanel `aria-controls`/`aria-labelledby` round-tripping. |
| `ZimmWishlistAuthDrawer` | `.../organisms/zimmWishlistAuthDrawer/index.tsx` | **Yes** | The best full precedent: `size="small" title={drawerTitle} finalFocusRef={triggerRef} initialFocusRef={emailInputRef}`. All logic in `useWishlistAuthDrawer`. |
| `ZimmAuthDrawerContent` | `.../organisms/zimmAuthDrawerContent/index.tsx` | **Yes** | Content-only (no dialog). Feature flags `socialEnabled` / `passwordlessEnabled` gate sections. Test mocks `zimmIcon`, `app/components/icons`, `zimmSocialButton`, `useUiCopy`; renders bare with `screen.*`, no portal. |
| `ZimmModal` | `.../ui-kits/atoms/zimmModal/index.tsx` | **No** | Props `{isOpen, mounted, onClose, maxWidth, labelledBy, describedBy?, children}`. `labelledBy` is **required**. Sets aria attrs imperatively via a state-backed callback ref because Chakra drops them — long comment explains the two-pass Portal mount. Story asserts `within(document.body).getByRole('dialog')` and waits `toHaveStyle({opacity:'1'})` before the a11y pass. |

**The Vitest portal-dialog answer:** `zimmWishlistAuthDrawer/index.test.tsx` does *not* render a real portal. It mocks the drawer away:

```tsx
// ZimmDrawer's own import chain is covered by zimmDrawer's own tests. Mock it to a minimal
// dialog stub so this suite can assert on open/close state without a full Chakra portal environment.
vi.mock('app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmDrawer', () => ({
  ZimmDrawer: ({ isOpen, onClose, children }) =>
    isOpen ? (<div role="dialog"><button onClick={onClose}>Close</button>{children}</div>) : null,
}));
```
then asserts with plain `screen.getByRole('dialog')` / `queryByRole`. That is the established pattern for testing a drawer *consumer* in Vitest.

## 3. Prop-selected named variants driving different copy + CTAs

**Best example — `ZimmProductCard`** (`/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.tsx`). A four-member discriminated union on `variation`, each member carrying its own required callbacks, plus a lookup table that drives every difference — explicitly *no* `switch` in the render body:

```ts
export type ZimmProductCardProps = ZimmProductCardBaseProps &
  (
    | ZimmProductCardPlpVariation
    | ZimmProductCardHomeVariation
    | ZimmProductCardWishlistVariation
    | ZimmProductCardRecentlyViewedVariation
  );
```
e.g. `ZimmProductCardWishlistVariation = { variation: 'wishlist'; colour: string; size: string; onRemove: () => void; onAddToBag?: () => void; ... }` vs `ZimmProductCardHomeVariation = { variation: 'home' }`. The table (line 391):
```ts
const VARIATION_CONFIG: Record<ZimmProductCardVariation, ZimmProductCardVariationConfig> = { home: {...}, plp: {...}, wishlist: {...}, recentlyViewed: {...} };
```
Its docblock states the intent: *"every layout/visibility decision this organism makes reads from this table, keyed by `variation` — adding a future variation means adding a union member above and one row here, touching no JSX."*

**Second example — `ZimmMediaTile`** (`.../atoms/zimmMediaTile/index.tsx`): `ZimmGalleryMediaItem = ZimmGalleryPhotoItem | ZimmGalleryVideoItem` discriminated on `kind: 'photo' | 'video'`, each with different required fields (`src`/`alt` vs `posterSrc`/`posterAlt`) and different controls.

Caveat: **no existing component drives different *copy strings* off a variant prop.** `VARIATION_CONFIG` is all booleans. The repo's convention is that microcopy comes from `useUiCopy()` / `useIntl()`, not props — stated explicitly in `zimmSubscribeSection/index.tsx`: *"Microcopy (labels, button text, status messages) comes from useUiCopy(), not props."* The closest thing to variant-selected copy is `useWishlistAuthDrawer` returning `drawerTitle` and `description` as computed strings (`overrides/app/hooks/useWishlistAuthDrawer.ts:311-312`), which the drawer then just renders.

The other `variant` props in `overrides/` are purely visual and live in `.css.ts` recipes: `ZimmButton` `'primary' | 'secondary' | 'social' | 'icon'`, `ZimmNavItem` `'light' | 'inverse' | 'sizeGuide' | 'sizeGuideLink'`, `ZimmDropdown` `'flush' | 'outline'`, `ZimmColourSwatch(Group)` `'square' | 'circle'`, `ZimmLogo` `'inverse' | 'default'`.

## 4. Cookie / storage suppression of a prompt

**No "don't show again" / dismissal-persistence precedent exists anywhere in `overrides/`.** No cookie library either — zero `document.cookie`, `js-cookie`, `Cookies.`, or cookie dependency in `package.json`. Grep for `dismissed|suppress|dontShow|hasSeen|firstVisit` returns only unrelated visual-suppression comments.

Two storage precedents do exist, both `sessionStorage` via the SFCC base helper `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/utils/utils`:

- `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/hooks/useWishlistAuthDrawer.ts:37` — `const PENDING_WISHLIST_INTENT_KEY = 'zimmPendingWishlistAction';` with `getSessionJSONItem` / `setSessionJSONItem` / `clearSessionJSONItem`, a `{intentId, timestamp}` payload, and a TTL that "transparently discard[s] (and clear[s]) one that's aged out". This is the closest structural analogue to a suppression key.
- `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/hooks/useRecentlyViewedHistory.ts:121` — `const storage = isRegistered ? localStorage : sessionStorage;`, with documented try/catch for Safari private mode (*"browsing mode throws on both `sessionStorage` and `localStorage` access, not just on write"*).
- Also `.../atoms/zimmSearchInput/index.tsx:51` — `RECENT_SEARCH_KEY` via the same session helpers.

**Didomi: zero code.** It appears only in docs (`AGENTS.md:138`, `.docs/architecture.md`, `.docs/prd/regional.md`) and `.docs/memory/projectState.md:20` lists it as `Not started`. No consent-gating utility or hook exists to hang a prompt off.

## 5. Focus-trap / focus-ref usage

No `useFocusTrap` hook, no `focus-trap` package, no `returnFocusOnClose` anywhere. `useZimmModal` (`/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/hooks/useZimmModal.ts`) used to own a trap and is now deliberately inert — it returns `trapRef`/`firstFocusRef` purely for call-site compatibility: *"neither ref drives behaviour any more."*

Real call sites:
- `zimmDrawer/index.tsx:199` — `if (finalFocusRef) finalFocusRef.current?.focus();` in `onCloseComplete`; `initialFocusRef={initialFocusRef}` on `<Drawer>` (line 208); `<ModalFocusScope>` wrapping the content (138).
- `zimmWishlistAuthDrawer/index.tsx:66-67` — `finalFocusRef={triggerRef}` + `initialFocusRef={emailInputRef}`, and line 80 forwards the same `emailInputRef` into the content.
- `zimmAuthDrawerContent/index.tsx:61` — `inputRef={initialFocusRef}` onto `EmailForm`.
- `zimmTextInput/index.tsx:90` — merges its internal ref with a forwarded one, *"e.g. initialFocusRef on a containing ZimmDrawer."*
- `list-menu/list-menu-popover.tsx:130,193,265` — `const initialFocusRef = useRef<HTMLElement>(null);` passed to a Chakra Popover.
